  message: "Fixed jointly with INV-lumuh in PR (dev abf47e01a7). Same malformed-slot defect as Nim: d_lang.py's external/stdlib import fallback (process_import else-branch, when the module is not in module_registry) emitted d:?:{module}:module (4 slots, '?' path, no span), leaving module_path/src=<unknown> and vibe.d invisible to refine_frameworks (reads parts[1]) -> vibe-d false-demote on dub. Fix: emit the canonical d:{module}:0-0:module:module form (module in parts[1]); in-tree imports already resolve to the real module symbol id (module_registry path, unchanged). Behavioral evidence (analyze_d): import vibe.vibe; -> d:vibe.vibe:0-0:module:module (parts[1]='vibe.vibe', was '?'). Extended package 100% coverage."  # ce3b
